course: dictionary
lesson: 7404
title: Poetry: words chosen for sound and picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Poetry is writing where the words are chosen for how they sound, how they move in a steady rhythm, and the pictures they make in your mind. «Rowing home in the evening sun, the Rat is murmuring poetry to himself.» Poems are often set out in short lines, and many of them rhyme, but not all of them do.
explain: Poetry can also mean a group of poems. You might say «a book of poetry» for a book full of poems, or talk about the poetry of one writer or one country. The word covers all of them together, so it is not usually used with «a» in front of it: you write a poem, but you study poetry.
explain: Poetry can describe beauty that is not writing at all. «The poetry of her dancing» means her dancing is graceful and lovely, like a good poem. When you see the word used this way, look for the feeling of beauty and grace, not for words on a page.
fact: Poetry is writing where words are chosen for their sound, rhythm and pictures.
fact: A single piece of poetry is called a poem.
fact: Free verse is poetry with no regular rhyme or beat, but the poet still breaks the lines where the reader should pause.
fact: «Poetry recital» means a performance where poems are read or spoken aloud.
fact: Poetry can describe grace in things that are not writing, such as dancing, as in «the poetry of her dancing».
exercise: «Rowing home in the evening sun, the Rat is murmuring poetry to himself.» What does poetry mean here? | A kind of small rowing boat | *Writing chosen for its sound, rhythm and pictures | A song sung loudly on the water | A map of the river
exercise: «Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat, but the poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause.» Why is free verse still poetry? | It is written in long paragraphs like a story | It always has a rhyme at the end of each line | *The words are chosen for sound and pictures, and the line breaks shape it | It has no words at all
exercise: Which phrase uses poetry to mean beauty in something that is not writing? | «a book of poetry» | «write poetry» | «a poetry recital» | *«the poetry of her dancing»
test: «Soon the Rat is scribbling poetry.» What is the Rat writing? | Sums for a maths lesson | Letters to the post office | *Poems | A shopping list
test: What does «a poetry recital» mean? | *A performance where poems are read or spoken aloud | A quiet test of spelling | A meeting about the harvest | A long walk through a forest
exam: Which statement about poetry is true? | It can only be found in very old books | *It uses sound, rhythm and pictures, and it does not always rhyme | It is always longer than a story | It must always rhyme at the end of every line
